{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202606141943401e95ffb756b14b23","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I've updated the fork seeding implementation. Now I need to wire the fork handler into the connector's `session_before_fork` hook in `index.ts`. \n\nLooking at the current `index.ts`, I can see that `session_before_fork` is registered as a `noop` handler. I need to implement the fork handling logic there.\n\nThe fork flow should be:\n1. On `session_before_fork`, detect the fork from the hook payload\n2. Create a new thread for the fork\n3. Seed the new thread by replaying source events up to the fork point\n4. The source thread receives no writes (verified by tests)\n\nLet me also think about the state management:\n- When a fork happens, we need to:\n  - Store the fork info (source thread, fork entryId)\n  - On the next `session_start` with reason \"fork\", we need to:\n    - Create a new thread\n    - Seed it from the source thread\n    - Update the connector's state to point to the new thread\n\nLooking at the PI types again, I see that `session_start` has a `reason` field that can be \"fork\", and `session_before_fork` gives us the fork point. \n\nThe flow should be:\n1. `session_before_fork` fires with the fork point (entryId, position)\n   - We capture this info for use on the next `session_start`\n2. `session_start` fires with reason \"fork\"\n   - We create a new thread\n   - We seed it from the source thread\n   - We initialize the instance against the new thread\n\nLet me implement this. First, I need to update the `index.ts` to handle `session_before_fork` and fork `session_start`.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4d7a60a-ad74-449d-9e1f-59d73cd3f78b","uuid":"a72becfd-00ad-4810-8e51-dda811378d14"}
